{"tool_name":"mokapot","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"mokapot","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/2020.12.01.407270"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Fast and flexible semi-supervised learning for peptide detection","home_url":"https://github.com/wfondrie/mokapot","keywords":["Proteomics","Peptides","Mass spectrometry"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":146},"biotools":{"id":"mokapot","home":"https://github.com/wfondrie/mokapot","summary":"Fast and Flexible Semisupervised Learning for Peptide Detection","addition_date":"2021-05-28T07:16:09Z","last_update_date":"2021-05-28T07:16:09Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:mokapot","cost":"Free of charge","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Protein identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3767"},{"term":"RNA-binding protein prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3901"}]}],"name":"mokapot","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/ACS.JPROTEOME.0C01010","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 The Authors. Published by American Chemical Society.Proteomics studies rely on the accurate assignment of peptides to the acquired tandem mass spectra - a task where machine learning algorithms have proven invaluable. We describe mokapot, which provides a flexible semisupervised learning algorithm that allows for highly customized analyses. We demonstrate some of the unique features of mokapot by improving the detection of RNA-cross-linked peptides from an analysis of RNA-binding proteins and increasing the consistency of peptide detection in a single-cell proteomics study.","authors":[{"name":"Fondrie W.E."},{"name":"Noble W.S."}],"date":"2021-04-02T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Proteome Research","title":"Mokapot: Fast and Flexible Semisupervised Learning